# 0-fault clusters of the hot group (LAYOUT-TEXT-PIN, D-X.63): <name> TAB <first key> TAB <last key>.
# Hand-kept (hot-text.list is generated). A cluster is every list position from its first key to its
# last; `cargo xtask so` aligns its first section to the smallest power of two not below its size, so
# it never straddles a 64 KiB fault-around window. Each starts with a function the earlier calls of its
# probe mode (page_faults.c) already ran, so the later call finds its text in a touched window.
# time: localtime_r's conversion (local_in) to the code only the first mktime runs (mode mktime).
# strings: the string kernels to the printf entry that runs first (mode strings); the printf body after it
# (vfprintf ...) is start-up text, at the list head since ruling #4417 (LAYOUT-TEXT-PIN-5); so is memmove,
# which start-up reaches through its entry labels (order.py --alias, #4467, LAYOUT-TEXT-PIN-6).
# rebind: bindtextdomain to the catalog lookup and the same-text check of a rebind (mode rebind), in two
# clusters of at most 32 KiB each (rebind, rebind-tail from catalog_of): one 38 KiB cluster took a 64 KiB
# alignment, which moved .text's start by 60 KiB and cost 52 KiB of gap ahead of it (ruling #4363).
# float: the first float conversion (mode float).
# @place end (LAYOUT-TEXT-PIN-4): the clusters, in this file's order, follow the last list position, so no
# alignment gap falls among the start-up and plain text (STARTUP-TEXT-WINDOWS) and the gaps sit side by
# side. `@place	in-place` keeps them at their list positions.
# Block on a window (LAYOUT-CLUSTER-WINDOW-ALIGN, D-X pending record): `so` starts the first cluster on a
# 64 KiB boundary, so the start-up tier's size moves the block by whole windows only and the windows below
# are this file's, not the tier's parity. With the clusters at most 32 KiB each (32 KiB aligned; float 16 KiB
# in the fast profile) the order pairs them into three windows, chosen by which probe paths open which:
#   [strings | rebind]: the coreutils-shaped path (mode tool: setlocale, bindtextdomain, textdomain, printf)
#     opens both (__printf_chk, bindtextdomain), so they cost it one window, not two; mode strings opens
#     strings and mode rebind opens rebind, each already its own window.
#   [time | rebind-tail]: no short-program path opens either; mode mktime / localtime_mktime open time and
#     mode rebind opens rebind-tail (catalog_of), each one window as before.
#   [float]: last, so the program's own .text (main), which every mode opens, follows it in its window.
# `so` prints the window of each cluster ("hot-text cluster block"). Keep the order when adding a cluster:
# a new one goes where the paths that open it already open a window, or after float.
@place	end
strings	strlen	__printf_chk
rebind	bindtextdomain	_RNCINvNtC13liella_legacy4intl9translateINtNtC15liella_boundary3sys8CSysImplKb0_ENtNtC15liella_boundary7catalog8CatalogsEs8_0C15liella_boundary
time	_RNvNtC15liella_boundary4zone8local_in	_RNvNtNtC6liella4time5civil17days_from_civil64
rebind-tail	_RINvNtC13liella_legacy4intl10catalog_ofINtNtC15liella_boundary3sys8CSysImplKb0_ENtNtC15liella_boundary7catalog8CatalogsEC15liella_boundary	_RNvMNtNtC6liella7catalog2moNtNtNtC6liella7catalog2mo2Mo4form
float	_RINvNtC6liella6printf12simple_floatNtNtC15liella_boundary6printf8ToBufferEC15liella_boundary	_RINvNtNtC6liella3num6format14decimal_stylesKjb0_EC6liella
